.TH updatenews 8 "June 2004"
.SH NAME
updatenews \- post articles from outgoing spool directory and prefetch newsgroups
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B updatenews
.RI "[\-h] [\-v] [\-c config-file] [\-a] [\-g] [\-o] [\-l] [\-w n]"
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
Updatenews  submits  all those articles that have been stored within NewsCache's outgoing-queue. If necessary the ActiveDB will be updated (see the \-a option to force the update). Afterwards  retrieves all the articles from the newsgroups listed in the PrefetchFile (This can be configured in newscache.conf).  
.PP
Without any of \-a, \-g, \-o and \-l, updatenews works as with \-g.
Once one of them is given, it prefetches groups only with \-g or \-o:
\-a or \-l alone only posts the queue and refreshes the active
database.
.PP
The outgoing queue is the directory .artSpool in the spool. An article
stays there until a news server takes it; when no news server can be
reached, the rest of the queue is kept for the next run. Articles the
news servers refuse are moved to .badArticles, for the administrator.
Only one updatenews at a time posts the queue.
.PP
.\" TeX users may be more comfortable with the \fB<whatever>\fP and
.\" \fI<whatever>\fP escape sequences to invode bold face and italics, 
.\" respectively.
.SH OPTIONS
These programs follow the usual GNU command line syntax, with long
options starting with two dashes (`-').
A summary of options is included below.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show summary of options.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show version of program.
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-configuration config-file
Read config-file instead of
.IR @SYSCONFDIR@/newscache.conf .
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-active
Force the prefetch the active data base. Updatenews first invalidate the ActiveDB to force the update.
.TP
.B \-g, \-\-group
Prefetch whole newsgroups (the articles of the newest 10000000 article numbers of each group).
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-over
Only prefetch the overview database (of the newest 10000000 article numbers of each group). With \-g as well, \-g wins.
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-lock-group, \-\-lock-groups
Always  lock  the newsgroup while prefetching it (with \-g). This improves the performance of update- news slightly, but nobody else can read this newsgroup while prefetching.
.TP
.B \-w, \-\-workers n
Accepted for old command lines and ignored (with a log line): updatenews
prefetches one newsgroup at a time. Older versions refused the option
with the usage text, so updatenews did nothing.

.SH PREFETCH FILE
Each line of the PrefetchFile is one of:
.TP
.I group.name
Prefetch this newsgroup.
.TP
.I pattern
A wildmat pattern with
.BR * ", " ? " or " [...] :
prefetch every group of the active database that matches it, in
alphabetical order.
.TP
.BI ! pattern
Don't prefetch the groups that match the pattern (or the group name),
wherever they come from in the file.
.PP
Empty lines and lines starting with # are skipped. Each group is
prefetched once, in the order of the file. Example:
.PP
.nf
# all of de.*, but not the binaries
de.*
!de.alt.binaries.*
comp.lang.[cg]o
at.test
.fi

.SH FILES
@SYSCONFDIR@/newscache.conf
.br
@SBINDIR@/newscache
.br
@SBINDIR@/newscacheclean
.br
@SBINDIR@/updatenews

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR newscache (8),
.BR newscache.conf (5),
.BR newscacheclean (8).
